LJ4 replay 1
# statics_ltp_reorder (03 s8, 14 sB.7; LJ_STATIC_LTP_PER_CHANNEL, LJ_STATIC_LEVEL_SCALES_ALL; rig 14 sB.8 items 3, 10):
# slot 1.1 A = 1:1 100; slot 1.2 B = 1:1 240 and 1:2 255 at level 50 % (120 / 128); slot 2.1 C = 1:2 10 with rep=slot.
# A, B, A again, deactivate A, A back, deactivate B; a command level override; Release All; then C releases A (same
# slot row, other page) and leaves B; Release Page 2.
# NOTE 03 s8 / 11 C5 LTP: "the last activated entry has priority ... The LTP evaluation works even if multiple entries
#      are activated or deactivated"; every enable puts that entry at top priority (tick 2: A re-activated tops B).
# NOTE 03 s8 levels "scale 0-100% of all values in the entry regardless of channel type" (LJ_STATIC_LEVEL_SCALES_ALL,
#      (v * level + 50) / 100): 240 x 50 % = 120, 255 x 50 % = 128, 240 x 25 % = 60, 255 x 25 % = 64.
# NOTE STATIC_ACTIVATE b = level override (tick 6: level=25 over the slot's 50); the scope is the slot's own rep (c 0xFF).
# NOTE 14 sB.7 Replace Slot (LJ_REP_SLOT; lj_static_scope_hits "the same slot row on every page"; PROPOSAL rig 14 sB.8
#      item 3): tick 10 activates 2.1 and releases 1.1; tick 11 proves it (1:1 falls to rank 0, not back to A's 100).
# NOTE 11 F17 / LJ_STATICS_USE_FADETIME 0 and LJ_STATIC_RELEASE_SNAPS (rig M9): every step snaps.
# NOTE W1 fails this file at tick 0 (1:1 expected 100 got 0): STATIC_ACTIVATE / STATIC_DEACTIVATE are W2 kinds.
tick_us=25000
patch 1 profile=19 link=1 addr=1
profile 1 class1=intensity use_gm=1
patch 2 profile=19 link=1 addr=2
profile 2 class1=intensity use_gm=1
static 1.1 name="A" act=toggle rep=add ft=50 level=100
ch 1:1=100:S
static 1.2 name="B" act=toggle rep=add ft=50 level=50
ch 1:1=240:S 1:2=255:S
static 2.1 name="C" act=toggle rep=slot ft=50 level=100
ch 1:2=10:S
at 0 static_act 1.1
expect 0 1:1=100 layer=4
expect 0 1:2=0 layer=0
expect_view 0 statics_any=1
at 1 static_act 1.2
expect 1 1:1=120 1:2=128 layer=4
at 2 static_act 1.1
expect 2 1:1=100 1:2=128 layer=4
at 3 static_deact 1.1
expect 3 1:1=120 1:2=128 layer=4
at 4 static_act 1.1
expect 4 1:1=100 1:2=128
at 5 static_deact 1.2
expect 5 1:1=100 layer=4
expect 5 1:2=0 layer=0
at 6 static_act 1.2 level=25
expect 6 1:1=60 1:2=64 layer=4
at 7 static_deact all
expect 7 1:1=0 1:2=0 layer=0
expect_view 7 statics_any=0
at 8 static_act 1.1
at 9 static_act 1.2
expect 9 1:1=120 1:2=128
at 10 static_act 2.1
expect 10 1:1=120 1:2=10 layer=4
at 11 static_deact 1.2
expect 11 1:1=0 layer=0
expect 11 1:2=10 layer=4
at 12 static_deact page 2
expect 12 1:1=0 1:2=0 layer=0
expect_view 12 statics_any=0
